==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|brembel|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term|bræmbel|lang=ang}}, from earlier {{term|brǣmel|lang=ang}}, {{term|brēmel|lang=ang}}, from dialectal {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*brēmila-}} (compare West Frisian {{term|brommel|lang=fy}}, Flemish {{term|bramel|lang=vls}}, Low German {{term|Brummel|lang=nds}}), diminutive of {{term/t|gem-pro|*brēm-}} (compare English {{term|broom|lang=en}}). More at {{l|en|broom}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-bramble.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{IPA|/ˈbɹæmbəl/|lang=en}} 
* {{rhymes|æmbəl}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|British|lang=en}} Common [[blackberry]].
# {{context|US|lang=en}} Any of several closely related thorny plants in the genus ''[[Rubus]]'', including [[blackberry]] and [[raspberry]].
# Any [[thorny]] [[shrub]].
# A [[cocktail]] of [[gin]], [[lemon juice]], and [[blackberry]] [[liqueur]].

